expect(summary.meta.symbols).toEqual(['parseThing']);
```

The expected value is **`['parseThing']`** — the symbol from tree-sitter, not the model's hallucination. The test comment explains: *"Prose-side fields still come from the model — it is the only source for them. But spans (path/lines/symbol) are tree-sitter, never the model, because §9 only calls a span verifiable if D9 produced it."*

So the contract is: **model controls prose fields (decisions, open_questions, tests, artifacts), tree controls location fields (path, start_line, end_line, symbol).** The reason: hallucinated symbol names would break every rehydration pointer in the store.

